WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.168
In the last years of the Later Han, the court was in utter chaos, and the officials were deeply worried.

00:00:06.518 --> 00:00:10.766
The people had had enough of war and longed for a stable life.

00:00:11.116 --> 00:00:17.284
The great general Guo Wei's conflict with the court deepened, and at last he led his soldiers in revolt.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:21.978
The soldiers' morale was high as they followed him forward.

00:00:22.328 --> 00:00:27.848
In the year 951, Guo Wei founded the Later Zhou, and the Later Han fell.

00:00:28.198 --> 00:00:34.246
After ascending the throne, Guo Wei carried out reforms, set the court in order, and the granaries gradually filled up.

00:00:34.596 --> 00:00:38.148
The people's lives gradually became stable.

00:00:38.498 --> 00:00:43.754
The young Chai Rong, at Guo Wei's side, earnestly learned the way of governing a state.

00:00:44.104 --> 00:00:49.144
He taught Chai Rong his experience of governing, bit by bit.

00:00:49.494 --> 00:00:56.358
Under their rule, the Later Zhou gradually grew strong, welcoming a brilliant rising sun.

00:00:56.708 --> 00:01:01.532
The people of the capital welcomed days of living and working in peace.

